    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a parabola of the form y = ax^2 + bx + c. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The parabola can be defined by specifying its two zeros and the value of its maximum (or minimum) point. Provides getters and setters for coefficients, as well as a method to evaluate the function at a given x. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
